From e053bc1fb8e1037edd7a9d92748df8b920ab9894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 13:47:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] mt-data-scope-callback: GORM tenant-scope callbacks + rdb
 tenant-scoped fallback + team composite uniqueness
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Installs the back-end half of the header-model multi-tenant story:

* framework/configstore/tenant_scope.go (new) — single registration of
  four GORM callbacks (Query/Update/Delete/Create). Reads tenant id from
  request context (under both the typed BifrostContextKey and the
  stringified fasthttp UserValue form), appends `<table>.tenant_id = ?`
  to every SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE on a tenant-scoped model, and stamps
  tenant_id on every INSERT row. Models without a TenantID column flow
  through untouched, so legacy upserts on plugins, logs, etc. are
  unaffected. The column is qualified with the primary table name so
  JOINs across two tenant-scoped tables (e.g. config_keys ->
  config_providers) don't throw "ambiguous column name: tenant_id".

* framework/configstore/sqlite.go + postgres.go — call
  RegisterTenantScopes(db) immediately after gorm.Open so every business
  query goes through the callbacks.

* framework/configstore/rdb.go — tenant-scope the config.json key-
  fallback lookup. Without this, a key created via the tenant-scoped
  admin API can be matched as the "existing" row for a startup-time
  config.json sync that writes a different tenant_id, then the Save()
  trips the composite (tenant_id, name) unique constraint.

* framework/configstore/tables/team.go — flip TableTeam.Name from a
  single-column uniqueIndex to composite (tenant_id, name) via
  idx_governance_teams_tenant_name. Two tenants can now both register
  a team called "engineering".

* migrationTenantScopedTeamNameUnique — drops the legacy
  idx_governance_teams_name and creates the composite. Idempotent
  (HasIndex guards both directions). On fresh DBs the composite is
  created by AutoMigrate via the struct tag.

* migrationUniqueTeamNames idempotency guard — must also skip the
  CreateIndex when the composite successor already exists. Without
  this, fresh-DB migration runs trip "index ... already exists".

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
